### MicroShop: try the API by hand.
### Open this file in Visual Studio 2022+, Rider, or VS Code with the REST Client extension
### and click "Send request" above each block. Start the system first: docker compose up --build

@gateway = http://localhost:5000
@keyboardId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@mouseId = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@monitorId = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
@cableId = 44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444

### Gateway root: lists the routes it knows
GET {{gateway}}/

### All products (gateway -> Catalog -> catalog-db)
GET {{gateway}}/api/products

### Two products in one call: what Orders does internally before accepting an order
GET {{gateway}}/api/products?ids={{keyboardId}}&ids={{mouseId}}

### Place an order -> 202 Accepted, status "Pending". Note the X-Trace-Id response header.
# @name placeOrder
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "ada@example.com",
  "items": [
    { "productId": "{{keyboardId}}", "quantity": 1 },
    { "productId": "{{mouseId}}", "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

### Run this about a second later: Pending -> Confirmed (eventual consistency)
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.$.id}}

### The "emails" Notifications sent for that order
GET {{gateway}}/api/notifications?orderId={{placeOrder.response.body.$.id}}

### Ask for more monitors than exist -> 202 now, Rejected a moment later
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "bob@example.com",
  "items": [ { "productId": "{{monitorId}}", "quantity": 10 } ]
}

### Unknown product -> 400 ValidationProblem straight away (checked synchronously with Catalog)
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "ada@example.com",
  "items": [ { "productId": "99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999", "quantity": 1 } ]
}

### Invalid request -> 400 from model validation (no service call at all)
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "not-an-email", "items": [] }

### Restock the monitor, then the order above would succeed
POST {{gateway}}/api/products/{{monitorId}}/restock
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 10 }

### Latest orders
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders

### ------------------------------------------------------------------ added for the web app

### Categories, for the shop's filter
GET {{gateway}}/api/products/categories

### One page of products in a category, optionally searching the name (category match ignores case)
GET {{gateway}}/api/products/search?category=accessories&q=&page=1&pageSize=12

### Create a product (category is required)
# @name createProduct
POST {{gateway}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Mechanical Numpad", "description": "Hot-swap switches", "price": 29.99, "initialStock": 5, "category": "Peripherals" }

### Edit it: name, description, price, category (stock only changes through restock and orders)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/products/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Mechanical Numpad v2", "description": "Hot-swap switches, USB-C", "price": 34.99, "category": "Peripherals" }

### Delete it -> 204
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/products/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}

### Health, straight to each service (these ports are exposed only for learning)
GET http://localhost:5101/health/ready

###
GET http://localhost:5102/health/ready

###
GET http://localhost:5103/health/ready
